say which operation ran, and which one never returned

iA Writer's library rows say Updating... forever, and nothing said whether the work behind them ran
at all. An operation whose main RAISES never reaches its isFinished, so it stays executing and
everything that depends on it waits: that failure and a merely slow indexer look identical from
outside.

CIDER_TRACE_OPS prints four lines per operation: added with whether it is ready, start, main, and
returned. A concurrent operation, which overrides start and finishes later on its own, shows start
with no main, which is why after-start prints whether it is finished or STILL RUNNING. The main
call is wrapped so a raise names the operation and the exception before it is rethrown, and the
rethrow keeps the behaviour exactly as it was.

WHAT IT SAID ON THE FIRST RUN, and it is what found the defect fixed in 0070:

  CIDER_OP added IALibraryIndexingOperation ready
  CIDER_OP start IALibraryIndexingOperation
  CIDER_OP after-start IALibraryIndexingOperation STILL RUNNING

Three lines, and no fourth. Then the run terminated on an unrecognized selector in the unarchiver.

Bounded at 400 lines and gated.
